#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198378 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198020 :question/id #uuid "9a1112c0-db94-5572-ba53-b78116b7c273" :question/math-academy-id "e-12355" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z) =\\left\\langle x+y,\\: x-y,\\: xyz \\right\\rangle, \\quad \\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u^2,\\: v^2 ,\\: 1 \\right\\rangle, \\quad (u,v)\\in D\\subset \\mathbb{R}^2.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $\\mathbf F$ across $S$ with respect to $\\mathbf{n}$ is given by\n\n![](images/d7/d7b8d89cae048a9cd5e04299bebdcb3a5d5d21ac6d5a31c48482aa00ca71517c.svg)\n\nwhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2v & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,4uv⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x+y,\\,x-y,\\,xyz⟩{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y={v}^{2}\\,z=1} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2}+{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,0,\\,4uv⟩ \\\\  & =({u}^{2}+{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\cdot 0+{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\cdot 4uv \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,4{u}^{3}{v}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e9b46ce4-cfe0-5da6-bc91-65ae8c544393" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050188 :topic/math-academy-id 3178 :topic/title "Flux in Three-Dimensional Vector Fields"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050508 :topic/math-academy-id 3386 :topic/title "Surface Integrals Over Parametric Surfaces"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198584 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94132937-eda0-5e90-a5ac-7f0f9def7aae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194136} {:answer/id #uuid "f7544775-c055-5b3c-895a-3510daf49d04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194137} {:answer/id #uuid "45e9bfa2-b5ab-5fb6-8215-c0e7746dd7cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194138} {:answer/id #uuid "47bb57ce-704e-5663-89a6-934af702d9e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194139} {:answer/id #uuid "608267cb-3d68-525c-bb1c-ef2ceab4fd7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94132937-eda0-5e90-a5ac-7f0f9def7aae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194136} :answer-field/id #uuid "977eb979-4b50-5a03-b91d-aa19a8c0611f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194135}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d6a0f062-0f76-50a3-a357-dfc6f1a08d98" :question/math-academy-id "q-160839" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨xz,\\,2y,\\,1⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨uv,\\,u+v,\\,1-v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}au{v}^{2}+b{v}^{2}+cuv-u+v\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨v,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ v & 1 & 0 \\\\ u & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}v & 0 \\\\ u & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}v & 1 \\\\ u & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,v,v-u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨xz,\\,2y,\\,1⟩{|}_{x=uv\\,y=u+v\\,z=1-v} \\\\  & =⟨uv\\cdot (1-v),\\,2(u+v),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨uv-u{v}^{2},\\,2u+2v,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨uv-u{v}^{2},\\,2u+2v,\\,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,v,\\,v-u⟩ \\\\  & =(uv-u{v}^{2})\\cdot (-1)+(2u+2v)\\cdot v+1\\cdot (v-u) \\\\  & =u{v}^{2}-uv+2uv+2{v}^{2}+v-u \\\\  & =u{v}^{2}+2{v}^{2}+uv-u+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\cdot u{v}^{2}+2\\cdot {v}^{2}+1\\cdot uv-u+v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+2+1=4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198585 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194750cf-4b33-5153-97c1-bd1b0f21c3c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u{v}^{3}+8{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275713} {:answer/id #uuid "30772c46-8461-5daa-94aa-ff5b8a754f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275909} {:answer/id #uuid "45100deb-1ec8-5bbb-b0b4-3c26c5616332" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u{v}^{3}+4{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276086} {:answer/id #uuid "45e6001c-4deb-5a8c-b01f-01531e4489d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4u{v}^{3}+2{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276094} {:answer/id #uuid "936bab95-9822-587d-80ac-54eded632448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276811}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "936bab95-9822-587d-80ac-54eded632448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{u}^{3}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276811} :answer-field/id #uuid "f81d9840-6037-5557-81d1-599235b0ea5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278161}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9fcf8673-a62b-588a-8020-ca78007689b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160840" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨-{u}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2x+y,\\,2z,\\,y+z⟩{|}_{x=-{u}^{2}\\,y=2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2(-{u}^{2})+(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}),\\,2({v}^{2}),\\,(2{u}^{2}-{v}^{2})+{v}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-{v}^{2},\\,2{v}^{2},\\,2{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨8uv,\\,4uv,\\,4uv⟩ \\\\  & =(-{v}^{2})\\cdot 8uv+2{v}^{2}\\cdot 4uv+2{u}^{2}\\cdot 4uv \\\\  & =-8u{v}^{3}+8u{v}^{3}+8{u}^{3}v \\\\  & =8{u}^{3}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,8{u}^{3}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1761d05c-b47b-569a-b7b6-4ed471f6dadf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275697} {:answer/id #uuid "40392ee9-b3f1-5009-bd69-fc1a719298c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{3}v+u{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276036} {:answer/id #uuid "66d47ff6-4d2f-51dd-a0bd-fe3a8ddbdd70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{u}^{3}v-2u{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276396} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d10ecc-5a2a-5169-bb03-eaafe2a1f99a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277369} {:answer/id #uuid "da347498-a4dc-5e22-9cb1-7985c24efdcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}v-2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+u{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1761d05c-b47b-569a-b7b6-4ed471f6dadf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275697} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9c299fe-08c9-5f88-b42b-ca47c7784874" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278018}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a99addda-c910-54da-a8cb-ae3a5ce916a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161249" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨2x,\\,2y,\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,-uv,\\,{v}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-4uv,\\,-2{u}^{2}⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-4uv,\\,-2{u}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2x,\\,2y,\\,z⟩{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=-uv\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨2{u}^{2},\\,-2uv,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2{u}^{2},\\,-2uv,\\,{v}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-4uv,\\,-2{u}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}\\cdot (-2{v}^{2})+(-2uv)\\cdot (-4uv)+{v}^{2}\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}) \\\\  & =-4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+8{u}^{2}{v}^{2}-2{u}^{2}{v}^{2} \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278470 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4065be-6410-5ccf-b764-e323b3954972" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275595} {:answer/id #uuid "996e1145-cf3a-5420-96fd-aafd97d1eb20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276855} {:answer/id #uuid "9f1089df-e42d-5caa-8e67-1152d56ad3b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276907} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e32ea5-a6f3-52a4-b8ec-13ac55fa6f7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277004} {:answer/id #uuid "dedf319d-2d9f-52cc-bda0-79efe3637268" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277425}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f1089df-e42d-5caa-8e67-1152d56ad3b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276907} :answer-field/id #uuid "e799dfb7-bba2-57d2-9a73-5392e0c83466" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278129}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2d1066e-0b79-5532-9ae3-4e710fbc5bc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161303" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,{u}^{2}+2v,\\,{u}^{3}+3v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}a{u}^{2}+bu+c\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{3}+3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2u,\\,3{u}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}+2v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{3}+3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2,\\,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2u & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2u & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2u \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6u-6{u}^{2},\\,3{u}^{2}-3,\\,2-2u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩{|}_{x=u+v\\,y={u}^{2}+2v\\,z={u}^{3}+3v} \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩\\cdot ⟨6u-6{u}^{2},\\,3{u}^{2}-3,\\,2-2u⟩ \\\\  & =1\\cdot (6u-6{u}^{2})+0\\cdot (3{u}^{2}-3)+2\\cdot (2-2u) \\\\  & =6u-6{u}^{2}+4-4u \\\\  & =-6{u}^{2}+2u+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-6)\\cdot {u}^{2}+2\\cdot u+4\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=-6+2+4=0.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278471 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd609ae-e864-57b8-94a4-273742d368ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275735} {:answer/id #uuid "2ccb8e67-96de-5752-b3c3-d11e0af4993a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275881} {:answer/id #uuid "54d35ae5-86bd-5395-8972-05d0d8d00e47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276231} {:answer/id #uuid "af78fb93-58e2-566e-a85b-fc76c0f645fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277047} {:answer/id #uuid "f88b3e2e-dffa-5fc2-9b42-e62568668267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54d35ae5-86bd-5395-8972-05d0d8d00e47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276231} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8a58223-7188-508a-9949-c05e00640b00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278051}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ba2bc0a-f01f-56b1-8fa8-5c3da0d50d17" :question/math-academy-id "q-161306" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨x-\\frac{1}{z},\\,y+\\frac{1}{z},\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u{e}^{v},\\,u{e}^{-v},\\,u⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}a{e}^{v}+b{e}^{-v}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{e}^{v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u{e}^{-v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{v},\\,{e}^{-v},\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{e}^{v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u{e}^{-v}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u{e}^{v},\\,-u{e}^{-v},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {e}^{v} & {e}^{-v} & 1 \\\\ u{e}^{v} & -u{e}^{-v} & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-v} & 1 \\\\ -u{e}^{-v} & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{v} & 1 \\\\ u{e}^{v} & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{v} & {e}^{-v} \\\\ u{e}^{v} & -u{e}^{-v}\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u{e}^{-v},\\,u{e}^{v},\\,-2u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x-\\frac{1}{z},\\,y+\\frac{1}{z},\\,z⟩{|}_{x=u{e}^{v}\\,y=u{e}^{-v}\\,z=u} \\\\  & =⟨u{e}^{v}-\\frac{1}{u},\\,u{e}^{-v}+\\frac{1}{u},\\,u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u{e}^{v}-\\frac{1}{u},\\,u{e}^{-v}+\\frac{1}{u},\\,u⟩\\cdot ⟨u{e}^{-v},\\,u{e}^{v},\\,-2u⟩ \\\\  & =(u{e}^{v}-\\frac{1}{u})\\cdot u{e}^{-v}+(u{e}^{-v}+\\frac{1}{u})\\cdot u{e}^{v}+u\\cdot (-2u) \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-{e}^{-v}+{u}^{2}+{e}^{v}-2{u}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{v}-{e}^{-v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\cdot {e}^{v}+(-1)\\cdot {e}^{-v}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=1-1=0.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d1c9dba-209f-56b2-8f1b-b1d0237d58ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275746} {:answer/id #uuid "26a5678b-7a2d-5817-8c83-9403924b91f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275827} {:answer/id #uuid "aff51ef5-48b1-5e4e-9bc6-f47b5b3b48de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}+uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277052} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d084df-38e6-570e-8bc2-f410786a2b67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277104} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c454d4-ce80-5860-8edf-68c01e34fae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1c454d4-ce80-5860-8edf-68c01e34fae3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277198} :answer-field/id #uuid "1900b165-70c5-5f9d-ad38-9a5a829338e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277771}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92e0422d-8551-525d-a92c-4ab1ea25fb60" :question/math-academy-id "q-161384" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{z}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,x⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,v,\\,u⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨{z}^{2},\\,{y}^{2},\\,x⟩{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=u} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩ \\\\  & ={u}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+{v}^{2}\\cdot 0+{u}^{2}\\cdot 2u \\\\  & =2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2{u}^{3}-{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d89472a-c8a6-58ee-ad06-702bb85242bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398509} {:answer/id #uuid "6ceed292-fdb3-5c81-a5ef-e21d4577bafc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\operatorname{cos}⁡v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398510} {:answer/id #uuid "2e773ddf-4b3c-5bc1-b538-c1702b36529f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\operatorname{cos}⁡v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398511} {:answer/id #uuid "06d6268a-1fe9-5430-934f-527eb0153af9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398512} {:answer/id #uuid "c1b5545b-f437-5265-821f-6ea217aea603" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06d6268a-1fe9-5430-934f-527eb0153af9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398512} :answer-field/id #uuid "f48bed04-e645-581d-90b2-d43b8caed324" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398508}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "50f21d4c-115f-5f6b-a6fe-50fa77f7169e" :question/math-academy-id "q-161251" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨3x,\\,3y,\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨3x,\\,3y,\\,z⟩{|}_{x=u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\,y=u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\,z={u}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{u}^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u⟩ \\\\  & =3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)+3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\cdot (-2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)+{u}^{2}\\cdot u \\\\  & =-6{u}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡v+{sin}^{2}⁡v)+{u}^{3} \\\\  & =-5{u}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,-5{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398534 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f13cf51-1f17-54c3-b3d0-3a4ed9f6cc76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398536} {:answer/id #uuid "0823e1c6-a66c-59c3-bb60-2b11710017b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}-{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398537} {:answer/id #uuid "7a803047-69b8-53fa-8d05-7893832957a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}{v}^{2}-2uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398538} {:answer/id #uuid "3330207b-8637-52ec-b488-bd1a488b22dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}+uv+2{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398539} {:answer/id #uuid "915a87fb-c1cd-571b-be39-7c31f1761641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}-uv+{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "915a87fb-c1cd-571b-be39-7c31f1761641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u{v}^{2}-uv+{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398540} :answer-field/id #uuid "af2f16f5-115b-5596-b71d-8a4dab14117a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398535}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd17085b-48fe-5be2-bc57-b62ce4e45b8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161383" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨xz,\\,y,\\,xz⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,uv,\\,v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨v,\\,-1,\\,u⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨v,\\,-1,\\,u⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨xz,\\,y,\\,xz⟩{|}_{x=u\\,y=uv\\,z=v} \\\\  & =⟨uv,\\,uv,\\,uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨uv,\\,uv,\\,uv⟩\\cdot ⟨v,\\,-1,\\,u⟩ \\\\  & =uv\\cdot v+uv\\cdot (-1)+uv\\cdot u \\\\  & =u{v}^{2}-uv+{u}^{2}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,u{v}^{2}-uv+{u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421783 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "189bee50-4a99-5b40-af14-d79a6be4cf78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421767} {:answer/id #uuid "1ab31c93-1b65-5e8b-a761-9f8a56bd7091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421768} {:answer/id #uuid "936a7baa-180a-5ac4-87b7-254a0a451cae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421773} {:answer/id #uuid "9c1d5f42-e69e-5804-8ffc-1ba7c0a90d40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421774} {:answer/id #uuid "a21a5496-3418-514f-ae65-4dd4f8f20907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ab31c93-1b65-5e8b-a761-9f8a56bd7091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421768} :answer-field/id #uuid "44498254-f6d6-5947-a33a-02e052e8e1fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421780}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27b29e44-b12e-5311-b5aa-28b3cb92f7e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161304" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨{x}^{2},\\,xy,\\,z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2uv⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}auv+b{u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}2uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2v \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2v \\\\ 1 & 2u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2v \\\\ 0 & 2u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2v,\\,-2u,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨{x}^{2},\\,xy,\\,z⟩{|}_{x=u\\,y=v\\,z=2uv} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,uv,\\,2uv⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨{u}^{2},\\,uv,\\,2uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-2v,\\,-2u,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & ={u}^{2}\\cdot (-2v)+uv\\cdot (-2u)+2uv\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2{u}^{2}v-2{u}^{2}v+2uv \\\\  & =2uv-4{u}^{2}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\cdot uv+(-4)\\cdot {u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=2-4=-2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02b1374a-677b-550b-816a-6cbd02c5f061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434818} {:answer/id #uuid "29ead56c-2949-5fb0-8895-cdd6a87df4b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434820} {:answer/id #uuid "bb3bf5e7-fb1f-5845-863a-15bfb2564e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434824} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e03b7e-e933-5e07-a534-f79399c89baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434825} {:answer/id #uuid "c757d8e1-3c0b-5fc9-9360-e929a186b1fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434826}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29ead56c-2949-5fb0-8895-cdd6a87df4b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434820} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1855324-ee18-529c-ba15-53c93565cb17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434829}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "22bda1b7-731c-5be9-8f1b-6668d9e068b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161253" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,xz,\\,yz⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{u}^{2},\\,v⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}auv+b{u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2u,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2u \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,-1,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,xz,\\,yz⟩{|}_{x=u\\,y={u}^{2}\\,z=v} \\\\  & =⟨v,\\,uv,\\,{u}^{2}v⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨v,\\,uv,\\,{u}^{2}v⟩\\cdot ⟨2u,\\,-1,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =v\\cdot 2u+uv\\cdot (-1)+{u}^{2}v\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2uv-uv+0 \\\\  & =uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}1\\cdot uv+0\\cdot {u}^{2}v\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=1+0=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501152 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "620afa66-2c6c-57b7-a3ae-d62a79f7f8f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{u}^{3}{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500671} {:answer/id #uuid "6ebe624d-df33-5b1a-ac75-393b05dce501" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{u}^{3}{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500692} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd3bc80-2dcb-5963-9f05-c0a968725eba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}{v}^{2}(3u+2v)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500784} {:answer/id #uuid "c2689dcd-d1d7-54f8-a7ca-f907d83e79ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}(uv+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500873} {:answer/id #uuid "f99ddd32-d363-5197-81ba-b8f06c983f5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{u}^{2}{v}^{2}(u+v)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "620afa66-2c6c-57b7-a3ae-d62a79f7f8f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{u}^{3}{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500671} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fefe9c8-5fc6-5bbb-bfe2-94890c45b24c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501042}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2343ccc6-302e-57d1-903e-91d537e6ff5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161385" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨-2x,\\,-2y,\\,-z⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{3},\\,{v}^{3},\\,uv⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-3{v}^{3},\\,-3{u}^{3},\\,9{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice we are told that the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}=⟨-3{v}^{3},\\,-3{u}^{3},\\,9{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨-2x,\\,-2y,\\,-z⟩{|}_{x={u}^{3}\\,y={v}^{3}\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =⟨-2{u}^{3},\\,-2{v}^{3},\\,-uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-2{u}^{3},\\,-2{v}^{3},\\,-uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-3{v}^{3},\\,-3{u}^{3},\\,9{u}^{2}{v}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =(-2{u}^{3})\\cdot (-3{v}^{3})+(-2{v}^{3})\\cdot (-3{u}^{3})+(-uv)\\cdot 9{u}^{2}{v}^{2} \\\\  & =6{u}^{3}{v}^{3}+6{u}^{3}{v}^{3}-9{u}^{3}{v}^{3} \\\\  & =3{u}^{3}{v}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,3{u}^{3}{v}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186549979 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67d2eb68-0652-5e48-b001-a45c2700c7e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549515} {:answer/id #uuid "94798f5c-574c-53cd-bb0e-eb9396410fae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549605} {:answer/id #uuid "c199e1eb-7983-554d-81aa-b675e5252dbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549680} {:answer/id #uuid "e8394076-ef1d-5d29-b139-67414f969f56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549743} {:answer/id #uuid "ee167035-8819-5d49-80a8-31c9bebffaab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67d2eb68-0652-5e48-b001-a45c2700c7e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549515} :answer-field/id #uuid "63772144-9630-582a-8d79-f08320bc64ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186549842}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8e8e30b7-68c9-50ac-bfbf-42853c6a4c1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-161305" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨x,\\,y,\\,xz⟩,\\,r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,uv⟩,\\,(u,v)\\in D⊂{R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{D}a{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+bu{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & v \\\\ 0 & 2v & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & v \\\\ 2v & u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-u,\\,2v⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x,\\,y,\\,xz⟩{|}_{x=u\\,y={v}^{2}\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =⟨u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}v⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,{u}^{2}v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-u,\\,2v⟩ \\\\  & =u\\cdot (-2{v}^{2})+{v}^{2}\\cdot (-u)+{u}^{2}v\\cdot 2v \\\\  & =-2u{v}^{2}-u{v}^{2}+2{u}^{2}{v}^{2} \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}-3u{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\cdot {u}^{2}{v}^{2}+(-3)\\cdot u{v}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=2-3=-1.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Through a Surface as a Double Integral"}]}
